  "method": "Actual installed Common session runtime and Squish codec. One-second warmup followed by four measured seconds per scene; synthetic clock advances at the declared game tick rate. Each world uses its densest board by authored peg count. Active shots use normal physics and automatic ordinary firing; later shots/retries may occur. Menus and paused scenes are also measured for needless repeat work. Payload counts only byte-distinct frames, modeling duplicate suppression for one remote self-hosted player. Browser-local solo play has no remote frame upload. Timings include tick, scene generation, serialization, one player buffer and byte comparison; exclude transport overhead, loading, browser rendering, mobile hardware and WAN. Asset bytes are raw media, excluding encoding/protocol overhead. This is not a capacity claim.",
